1. Home Assistant core - "ecovacs" integration
-----------------------------------------------
Source:  https://github.com/home-assistant/core
         homeassistant/components/ecovacs at tag 2026.11.2
License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE)
Copyright: The Home Assistant authors

Used in: __init__.py, binary_sensor.py, button.py, config_flow.py, const.py,
controller.py, diagnostics.py, entity.py, event.py, icons.json, image.py,
lawn_mower.py, number.py, select.py, sensor.py, services.py, services.yaml,
strings.json, switch.py, translations/en.json, translations/nl.json, util.py,
vacuum.py (all under custom_components/ecovacs_t90s/).

The files were modified: the legacy XMPP (py-sucks) robot support was
removed, the domain was renamed to ecovacs_t90s, extra device classes are
registered before discovery, the live view entities and options were added,
a raw_command service was added, and (version 0.2.0) the vacuum uses the V2
clean commands with a local Matter fallback, the map shows furniture, and
entities for further robot settings were added. The English texts are the
resolved texts of the core integration, some Dutch texts are taken from the
Home Assistant translations of that integration.


